    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's exactly what i'm seeing. it's so calculated. i've noticed another one used a ton in political speeches: \"it is important to remember.\" it's always used when they're about to say something that actually contradicts what they just said or what people know to be true. it's like they're trying to overwrite the listener's memory in real-time. if we're building this catalog, how would you classify that one? it feels like it's more about cognitive overriding than just redirection.",
